hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22863","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us: Zaidah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Shaqiq: Samurah ibn Sahm narrated to us, who said: I stayed with Abu Hashim ibn Utbah while he was wounded. So Muawiyah came to him visiting him, and he wept. So Muawiyah said to him: What makes you weep? Is it pain distressing you, or for this world, for its best has gone? He said: For neither at all, but the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entrusted to me a trust, and I wish I had followed it. Indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Perhaps you will see wealth divided among people, and indeed sufficient for you of gathering wealth is a servant and a mount in the path of Allah, exalted. So I found, and I gathered."
